#: source/refs/contributing.rst:2
msgid "Contribution Guidelines"
msgstr "贡献指南"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:6
msgid ""
"This page is the source of truth for the ``isaaclab-following-coding-"
"style``, ``isaaclab-preparing-pr-workflow``, and ``isaaclab-writing-"
"changelog-fragments`` agent skills (`skills/developer/coding-style/ "
"<../../../skills/developer/coding-style/SKILL.md>`__, `skills/developer/pr-"
"workflow/ <../../../skills/developer/pr-workflow/SKILL.md>`__, "
"`skills/developer/changelog-fragments/ <../../../skills/developer/changelog-"
"fragments/SKILL.md>`__). When shared guidance changes, update affected skill"
" workflows and examples without copying the rules. See "
":doc:`/source/developer-tools/agent_skills`."
msgstr ""
"本页是 ``isaaclab-following-coding-style`` 、 ``isaaclab-preparing-pr-workflow``"
" 和 ``isaaclab-writing-changelog-fragments`` 智能体技能的权威依据（ "
"`skills/developer/coding-style/ <../../../skills/developer/coding-"
"style/SKILL.md>`__ 、 `skills/developer/pr-workflow/ "
"<../../../skills/developer/pr-workflow/SKILL.md>`__ 、 "
"`skills/developer/changelog-fragments/ <../../../skills/developer/changelog-"
"fragments/SKILL.md>`__ ）。共享指导改变时，应更新相关技能的工作流和示例，不要复制规则。参见 "
":doc:`/source/developer-tools/agent_skills` 。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:14
msgid ""
"We wholeheartedly welcome contributions to the project to make the framework"
" more mature and useful for everyone. These may happen in forms of:"
msgstr "我们衷心欢迎对项目的贡献，以使框架更加成熟并对大家更加有用。这些贡献可能以以下形式出现: "

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:17
msgid ""
"Bug reports: Please report any bugs you find in the `issue tracker "
"<https://github.com/isaac-sim/IsaacLab/issues>`__."
msgstr ""
"Bug 报告: 如果您发现任何 bug，请在 `issue tracker <https://github.com/isaac-"
"sim/IsaacLab/issues>`__ 中报告。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:18
msgid ""
"Feature requests: Please suggest new features you would like to see in the "
"`discussions <https://github.com/isaac-sim/IsaacLab/discussions>`__."
msgstr ""
"功能请求: 请提出您希望在 `discussions <https://github.com/isaac-"
"sim/IsaacLab/discussions>`__ 中看到的新功能。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:19
msgid ""
"Code contributions: Please submit a `pull request <https://github.com/isaac-"
"sim/IsaacLab/pulls>`__."
msgstr ""
"代码贡献: 请提交一个 `pull request <https://github.com/isaac-sim/IsaacLab/pulls>`__ 。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:21
msgid "Bug fixes"
msgstr "错误修复"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:22
msgid "New features"
msgstr "新特性"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:23
msgid "Documentation improvements"
msgstr "文档改进"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:24
msgid "Tutorials and tutorial improvements"
msgstr "教程和教程改进"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:26
msgid ""
"We prefer GitHub `discussions <https://github.com/isaac-"
"sim/IsaacLab/discussions>`_ for discussing ideas, asking questions, "
"conversations and requests for new features."
msgstr ""
"我们更倾向于使用 GitHub `discussions <https://github.com/isaac-"
"sim/IsaacLab/discussions>`_ 来讨论想法、提问、交流和新功能的请求。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:29
msgid ""
"Please use the `issue tracker <https://github.com/isaac-"
"sim/IsaacLab/issues>`_ only to track executable pieces of work with a "
"definite scope and a clear deliverable. These can be fixing bugs, new "
"features, or general updates."
msgstr ""
"请仅使用 `issue tracker <https://github.com/isaac-sim/IsaacLab/issues>`_ "
"来跟踪具有明确范围和清晰交付物的可执行任务。这些任务可以是修复 bug、新功能或一般更新。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:35
msgid "Contributing Code"
msgstr "贡献代码"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:39
msgid ""
"Please refer to the `Google Style Guide "
"<https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html>`__ for the coding style "
"before contributing to the codebase. In the coding style section, we outline"
" the specific deviations from the style guide that we follow in the "
"codebase."
msgstr ""
"请参阅 `Google Style Guide "
"<https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html>`__ "
"以了解编码风格，然后再为代码库做贡献。在编码风格部分，我们概述了代码库中遵循的与风格指南的具体偏差。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:43
msgid ""
"We use `GitHub <https://github.com/isaac-sim/IsaacLab>`__ for code hosting. "
"Please follow the following steps to contribute code:"
msgstr ""
"我们使用 `GitHub <https://github.com/isaac-sim/IsaacLab>`__ 进行代码托管。请按照以下步骤贡献代码: "

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:46
msgid ""
"Create an issue in the `issue tracker <https://github.com/isaac-"
"sim/IsaacLab/issues>`__ to discuss the changes or additions you would like "
"to make. This helps us to avoid duplicate work and to make sure that the "
"changes are aligned with the roadmap of the project."
msgstr ""
"在 `issue tracker <https://github.com/isaac-sim/IsaacLab/issues>`__ "
"中创建一个问题，讨论您希望进行的更改或添加内容。这有助于我们避免重复工作，并确保这些更改与项目的路线图保持一致。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:49
msgid "Fork the repository."
msgstr "Fork 仓库。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:50
msgid "Create a new branch for your changes."
msgstr "创建一个新分支用于您的更改。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:51
msgid "Make your changes and commit them."
msgstr "进行更改并提交它们。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:52
msgid "Push your changes to your fork."
msgstr "将您的更改推送到您的 fork。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:53
msgid ""
"Submit a pull request to the `develop branch <https://github.com/isaac-"
"sim/IsaacLab/compare/develop...>`__."
msgstr ""
"向 `develop 分支 <https://github.com/isaac-sim/IsaacLab/compare/develop...>`__ "
"提交 PR。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:54
msgid "Ensure all the checks on the pull request template are performed."
msgstr "确保对拉取请求模板执行所有检查。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:56
msgid ""
"After sending a pull request, the maintainers will review your code and "
"provide feedback."
msgstr "在发送拉取请求之后，维护者将审查你的代码并提供反馈。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:58
msgid ""
"Ensure that your code is formatted and documented, and run the relevant "
"tests and required CI checks as described in `Unit Testing`_ and `Tools`_."
msgstr ""
"确保代码格式正确、文档完整，并按 `单元测试 <Unit Testing_>`_ 和 `工具 <Tools_>`_ 所述，运行相关测试和必需的 CI "
"检查。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:63
msgid ""
"It is important to keep the pull request as small as possible. This makes it"
" easier for the maintainers to review your code. If you are making multiple "
"changes, please send multiple pull requests. Large pull requests are "
"difficult to review and may take a long time to merge."
msgstr ""
"保持拉取请求尽可能小是很重要的。这使得维护者更容易审查你的代码。如果你正在进行多个更改，请发送多个拉取请求。大型拉取请求很难审查，并且可能需要很长时间才能合并。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:68
msgid ""
"More details on the code style and testing can be found in the `Coding "
"Style`_ and `Unit Testing`_ sections."
msgstr "关于代码风格和测试的更多细节可以在 `代码风格`_ 和 `单元测试`_ 部分找到。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:72
msgid "Contributing Documentation"
msgstr "贡献文档"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:74
msgid ""
"Contributing to the documentation is as easy as contributing to the "
"codebase. All the source files for the documentation are located in the "
"``IsaacLab/docs`` directory. The documentation is written in "
"`reStructuredText <https://docutils.sourceforge.io/rst.html>`__ format."
msgstr ""
"为文档贡献的方式与为代码库贡献一样简单。所有文档的源文件都位于 ``IsaacLab/docs`` 目录中。文档使用 `reStructuredText"
" <https://docutils.sourceforge.io/rst.html>`__ 格式编写。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:78
msgid ""
"We use `Sphinx <https://www.sphinx-doc.org/en/master/>`__ with the `Book "
"Theme <https://sphinx-book-theme.readthedocs.io/en/stable/>`__ for "
"maintaining the documentation."
msgstr ""
"我们使用 `Sphinx <https://www.sphinx-doc.org/en/master/>`__ 和 `Book Theme "
"<https://sphinx-book-theme.readthedocs.io/en/stable/>`__ 来维护文档。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:82
msgid ""
"API ``[source]`` links open the implementation on GitHub, using the "
"published documentation's branch or tag (``develop`` for a current-checkout "
"build by default). We do not generate local Python source pages; viewing the"
" implementation requires internet access."
msgstr ""
"API 的 ``[source]`` 链接在 GitHub 上打开实现，使用发布文档对应的分支或标签；当前检出目录的构建默认为 ``develop`` "
"。我们不生成本地 Python 源码页，因此查看实现需要联网。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:86
msgid ""
"Sending a pull request for the documentation is the same as sending a pull "
"request for the codebase. Please follow the steps mentioned in the "
"`Contributing Code`_ section."
msgstr "发送文档的拉取请求与发送代码库的拉取请求相同。请按照 `贡献代码`_ 部分中提到的步骤进行操作。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:89
msgid ""
"For documentation media, only small ``.jpg`` files should be committed "
"directly to the Isaac Lab repository. Upload larger images, videos, "
"animations, and other media to an external hosting location, then link to or"
" embed the externally hosted file from the documentation."
msgstr ""
"文档媒体中，只有较小的 ``.jpg`` 文件应直接提交到 Isaac Lab "
"仓库。较大的图片、视频、动画等媒体，应上传到外部托管位置，再从文档链接或嵌入。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:95
msgid ""
"Install `uv <https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/>`__ "
"before building the documentation. The build command syncs the ``dev`` "
"extra, which includes documentation requirements, into the repository's "
"``.venv``."
msgstr ""
"构建文档前，先安装 `uv <https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/>`__ "
"。构建命令将包含文档依赖的 ``dev`` 可选依赖组同步到仓库的 ``.venv`` 。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:100
msgid "Choose documentation validation according to the changed behavior:"
msgstr "根据修改影响的行为，选择文档验证方式："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:102
msgid ""
"Skip Sphinx when rendered docs are unaffected, including standalone "
"``AGENTS.md`` and ``skills/`` edits. Run the relevant code or skill checks "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"渲染文档不受影响时，跳过 Sphinx，包括单独修改 ``AGENTS.md`` 或 ``skills/`` 的情况，改为运行相关代码或技能检查。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:104
msgid "Use the incremental HTML preview while editing documentation pages."
msgstr "编辑文档页时，使用增量 HTML 预览。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:105
msgid ""
"Use a clean build for API signatures or docstrings, Sphinx configuration or "
"extensions, and theme changes. Sphinx's cache does not reliably detect "
"Python source changes."
msgstr ""
"修改 API 签名、文档字符串、Sphinx 配置或扩展，以及主题时，使用全新构建；Sphinx 缓存不能可靠检测 Python 源码变更。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:107
msgid ""
"Run one clean, warning-free build of final documentation-affecting changes "
"before submitting a PR. Repeat it only after further relevant changes or a "
"failure. CI also runs the clean build."
msgstr ""
"提交 PR 前，对最终影响文档的修改执行一次全新构建，并确保没有警告。只有后续又有相关修改或构建失败时，才需要重复。CI 也会执行全新构建。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:110
msgid ""
"For an incremental HTML preview, run this command from the repository root "
"on Linux or Windows:"
msgstr "增量 HTML 预览在 Linux 和 Windows 上均从仓库根目录运行："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:116
msgid "On systems with Make, the equivalent command is:"
msgstr "有 Make 的系统可使用等价命令："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:122
msgid ""
"Open ``docs/_build/incremental/index.html`` to inspect the preview. "
"Subsequent runs reuse the cache and treat new warnings as errors, but can "
"omit old warnings and retain deleted pages. Use a clean build for final "
"validation, and avoid concurrent builds in the same output directory."
msgstr ""
"打开 ``docs/_build/incremental/index.html`` "
"查看预览。后续运行复用缓存，将新警告视为错误，但可能遗漏旧警告或保留已删除页面。最终验证应使用全新构建；不要向同一输出目录并发构建。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:126
msgid ""
"For the final clean build, run the following command from the repository "
"root. It installs the documentation packages and builds the current version:"
msgstr "最终全新构建从仓库根目录运行以下命令。它安装文档包，并构建当前版本："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:133
msgid ""
"The documentation is generated in ``docs/_build/current``. Open "
"``docs/_build/current/index.html`` in a browser to view it. Each build "
"clears the current HTML output and its Sphinx cache so deleted pages and "
"cached warnings cannot be carried over."
msgstr ""
"文档生成于 ``docs/_build/current`` 。在浏览器打开 ``docs/_build/current/index.html`` "
"查看。每次构建都会清空当前 HTML 输出和 Sphinx 缓存，避免保留已删除页面或缓存中的警告。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:139
msgid "Contributing assets"
msgstr "贡献资产"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:141
msgid ""
"Large asset files should not be added directly to the Isaac Lab repository. "
"Instead, host them in a separate repository and link to them from the "
"relevant documentation."
msgstr "大型资产文件不应直接加入 Isaac Lab 仓库，应托管在独立仓库，再从相关文档链接过去。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:144
msgid ""
"Please checkout the `Isaac Sim Assets "
"<https://docs.isaacsim.omniverse.nvidia.com/latest/assets/usd_assets_overview.html>`__"
" for more information on what is presently available."
msgstr ""
"请查看 `Isaac Sim 资产 "
"<https://docs.isaacsim.omniverse.nvidia.com/latest/assets/usd_assets_overview.html>`__"
" 以了解当前可用资源的更多信息。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:149
msgid ""
"We are currently working on a better way to contribute assets. We will "
"update this section once we have a solution. In the meantime, please follow "
"the steps mentioned below."
msgstr "我们目前正在研究一种更好的方式来贡献资产。一旦我们有了解决方案，我们将更新此部分。在此期间，请按照下面提到的步骤进行操作。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:152
msgid "To host your own assets, the current solution is:"
msgstr "要托管您自己的资源，当前的解决方案是: "

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:154
msgid "Create a separate repository for the assets and add it over there"
msgstr "创建一个单独的存储库用于资产，并将其添加到那里"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:155
msgid "Make sure the assets are licensed for use and distribution"
msgstr "确保资产已获得使用和分发的许可"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:156
msgid "Include images of the assets in the README file of the repository"
msgstr "在仓库的 README 文件中包含资产的图片"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:157
msgid "Send a pull request with a link to the repository"
msgstr "发送一个包含仓库链接的拉取请求"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:159
msgid ""
"We will then verify the assets and their licensing and determine how to "
"integrate them. If you have questions, please open an issue in the "
"repository."
msgstr "我们随后会验证资产及其许可，并确定集成方式。如有疑问，请在仓库提交 issue。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:164
msgid "Maintaining package changelogs and versions"
msgstr "维护包的变更日志与版本"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:166
msgid ""
"Each release-managed package maintains a changelog in ``docs/CHANGELOG.rst``"
" and its version in ``pyproject.toml``."
msgstr ""
"每个纳入发布管理的包，在 ``docs/CHANGELOG.rst`` 中维护变更日志，在 ``pyproject.toml`` 中维护版本。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:169
msgid ""
"The changelog contains the curated, chronologically ordered list of notable "
"changes for each package version."
msgstr "变更日志按时间顺序整理各包版本的重要变更。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:174
msgid ""
"``CHANGELOG.rst`` and the package version in ``pyproject.toml`` are compiled"
" nightly by CI from per-PR `towncrier <https://towncrier.readthedocs.io/>`__"
" **fragment files** — contributors do not edit them directly. For every "
"package your PR touches in ``source/<pkg>/`` (outside ``changelog.d/``), add"
" fragments under ``source/<pkg>/changelog.d/``:"
msgstr ""
"CI 每晚根据各 PR 的 `towncrier <https://towncrier.readthedocs.io/>`__ **片段文件** ，生成"
" ``CHANGELOG.rst`` 和 ``pyproject.toml`` 中的包版本；贡献者不直接编辑二者。对于 PR 修改的每个 "
"``source/<pkg>/`` 包（不计 ``changelog.d/`` ），在 ``source/<pkg>/changelog.d/`` "
"下添加片段："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:179
msgid ""
"``<slug>.<type>.rst`` — one file per entry type, where ``<type>`` is "
"``added``, ``changed``, ``deprecated``, ``removed`` or ``fixed``; the file "
"holds that section's bullets."
msgstr ""
"``<slug>.<type>.rst`` ：每种条目类型一个文件， ``<type>`` 为 ``added`` 、 ``changed`` 、 "
"``deprecated`` 、 ``removed`` 或 ``fixed`` ；文件包含对应章节的列表条目。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:181
msgid ""
"``<slug>.minor`` or ``<slug>.major`` — an empty file that raises the version"
" bump from patch to minor (new public API) or major (breaking change)."
msgstr ""
"``<slug>.minor`` 或 ``<slug>.major`` ：空文件，将版本升级级别从补丁级提高到次版本级（新增公共 "
"API）或主版本级（不兼容变更）。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:183
msgid ""
"``<slug>.skip`` — an empty file for no entry and no bump (CI / docs / test-"
"only PRs)."
msgstr "``<slug>.skip`` ：空文件，不生成条目也不升级版本，适用于只修改 CI、文档或测试的 PR。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:185
msgid ""
"``<slug>`` is any short, unique name; your branch name with ``/`` replaced "
"by ``-`` is the recommended default. Within a batch the highest tier wins "
"for the package. The package version in ``pyproject.toml`` is bumped by CI "
"according to `Semantic Versioning <https://semver.org/>`__."
msgstr ""
"``<slug>`` 可使用任意简短、唯一的名称；建议默认采用分支名，并将 ``/`` 替换为 ``-`` 。同一批次中，该包采用最高升级级别。CI 按"
" `语义化版本 <https://semver.org/>`__ 升级 ``pyproject.toml`` 中的包版本。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:190
msgid ""
"The changelog file is written in `reStructuredText "
"<https://docutils.sourceforge.io/rst.html>`__ format. The goal of this "
"changelog is to help users and contributors see precisely what notable "
"changes have been made between each release of a package. This is a *MUST* "
"for every release-managed package."
msgstr ""
"变更日志使用 `reStructuredText <https://docutils.sourceforge.io/rst.html>`__ "
"格式，帮助用户和贡献者准确了解各包版本之间的重要变更。每个纳入发布管理的包都 *必须* 提供变更日志。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:194
msgid "For each fragment, please follow the following guidelines:"
msgstr "编写各片段时，遵循以下指南："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:196
msgid ""
"Each fragment's ``<type>`` names the changelog section its bullets appear "
"under."
msgstr "各片段的 ``<type>`` 指定其条目所属的变更日志章节。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:198
msgid "``added``: For new features."
msgstr "``added`` ：新增功能。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:199
msgid "``changed``: For changes in existing functionality."
msgstr "``changed`` ：已有功能的变更。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:200
msgid "``deprecated``: For soon-to-be removed features."
msgstr "``deprecated`` ：即将移除的功能。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:201
msgid "``removed``: For now removed features."
msgstr "``removed`` ：已移除的功能。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:202
msgid "``fixed``: For any bug fixes."
msgstr "``fixed`` ：错误修复。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:204
msgid ""
"Each change is described with a ``*`` bullet point; continuation lines are "
"indented."
msgstr "每项变更使用 ``*`` 列表项描述，续行缩进。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:205
msgid ""
"Prefix breaking changes with **Breaking:** and provide migration guidance "
"for deprecated, changed, or removed behavior that requires callers to adapt."
msgstr "不兼容变更以 **Breaking:** 开头；对于调用方需要适配的弃用、变更或移除行为，提供迁移说明。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:207
msgid "The bullet points are written in the **past tense**."
msgstr "项目要点采用 **过去时** 编写。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:209
msgid "This means that the change is described as if it has already happened."
msgstr "这意味着这个变化被描述为已经发生过。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:210
msgid ""
"The bullet points should be concise and to the point. They should not be "
"verbose."
msgstr "项目要简明扼要，直奔主题。不应冗长。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:211
msgid ""
"The bullet point should also include the reason for the change, if "
"applicable."
msgstr "项目符号应当包括变更的原因，如果适用。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:216
msgid ""
"When in doubt, please check the style in the existing changelog files and "
"follow the same style."
msgstr "有疑问时，请检查现有的 changelog 文件中的样式，并遵循相同的样式。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:218
msgid ""
"For example, ``source/isaaclab/changelog.d/fix-partial-reset.fixed.rst``:"
msgstr "例如， ``source/isaaclab/changelog.d/fix-partial-reset.fixed.rst`` ："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:226
msgid "Coding Style"
msgstr "编码风格"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:228
msgid ""
"We follow the `Google Style Guides "
"<https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html>`__ for the codebase. For "
"Python code, the PEP guidelines are followed. Most important ones are `PEP-8"
" <https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0008/>`__ for code comments and "
"layout, `PEP-484 <http://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0484>`__ and `PEP-585 "
"<https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0585/>`__ for type-hinting."
msgstr ""
"我们遵循 `Google Style Guides "
"<https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html>`__ 作为代码库的规范。对于 Python "
"代码，遵循 PEP 指南。最重要的包括 `PEP-8 <https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0008/>`__ "
"用于代码注释和布局， `PEP-484 <http://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0484>`__ 和 `PEP-585 "
"<https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0585/>`__ 用于类型提示。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:237
msgid ""
"For documentation, we adopt the `Google Style Guide <https://sphinxcontrib-"
"napoleon.readthedocs.io/en/latest/example_google.html>`__ for docstrings. We"
" use `Sphinx <https://www.sphinx-doc.org/en/master/>`__ for generating the "
"documentation. Please make sure that your code is well-documented and "
"follows the guidelines."
msgstr ""
"对于文档，我们采用 `Google Style Guide <https://sphinxcontrib-"
"napoleon.readthedocs.io/en/latest/example_google.html>`__ 来编写 docstring。我们使用"
" `Sphinx <https://www.sphinx-doc.org/en/master/>`__ "
"来生成文档。请确保您的代码有良好的文档说明并遵循指南。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:242
msgid "Refactoring and API Design"
msgstr "重构与 API 设计"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:244
msgid ""
"Make the smallest change that solves the problem. Read surrounding code, "
"callers, tests, and documentation before changing an interface. Apply these "
"rules when adding code or cleaning up existing implementations:"
msgstr "采用能解决问题的最小修改。修改接口前，阅读周边代码、调用方、测试和文档。新增代码或整理现有实现时，遵循以下规则："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:247
msgid ""
"Preserve observable behavior unless the change explicitly requires "
"otherwise. Check ordering, shapes, dtype, device, input mutation, and "
"failure behavior as well as return values. Public API removals and renames "
"require a deprecation and migration path."
msgstr ""
"除非修改明确要求，否则保留可观察行为。除返回值外，还要检查顺序、形状、dtype、设备、输入修改和失败行为。移除或重命名公共 "
"API，需要弃用过程和迁移方式。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:250
msgid ""
"Prefer a functional approach for stateless computations and transformations:"
" use plain functions with explicit inputs and outputs, keeping side effects "
"at clear boundaries. Use classes when they own meaningful state or "
"resources, enforce invariants over a lifecycle, or implement an interface "
"required by the architecture. Avoid classes that only group static methods, "
"wrap a single operation, or forward calls to another object. Preserve "
"established public contracts when simplifying existing designs."
msgstr ""
"无状态计算与转换优先采用函数式方式：使用输入、输出明确的普通函数，将副作用放在清晰边界。需要持有实质状态或资源、在生命周期内维护不变量，或实现架构要求的接口时，使用类。避免仅为归组静态方法、包装单个操作或转发另一对象调用而建立类。简化现有设计时，保留既有公共约定。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:255
msgid ""
"Reuse existing mechanisms before introducing helpers, configuration options,"
" or abstractions. Extract shared logic when it has the same contract; keep "
"helpers private unless callers need a public API. Prefer direct control flow"
" and early returns when they remove unnecessary nesting."
msgstr ""
"引入辅助函数、配置选项或抽象前，先复用现有机制。共享逻辑约定相同时再提取；除非调用方需要公共 "
"API，否则辅助函数应保持私有。直接控制流和提前返回能减少不必要嵌套时，应优先使用。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:258
msgid ""
"Inline simple expressions and operations when a helper would only add "
"indirection. Do not extract a one-line helper merely to rename an obvious "
"operation. Introduce a helper when it removes meaningful duplication or "
"gives a coherent, non-trivial operation a useful name; its benefit should "
"outweigh the need to jump to another definition to understand the caller."
msgstr ""
"如果辅助函数只增加跳转层级，简单表达式和操作应直接写在调用处。不要仅为给显而易见的操作改名而提取单行函数。只有能消除实质重复，或为完整、非简单操作提供有用名称时，才引入辅助函数；收益应超过理解调用方时跳到另一处定义的成本。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:262
msgid ""
"Prefer direct attribute access and assignment (``obj.value`` and ``obj.value"
" = value``). Use ``getattr`` and ``setattr`` only when dynamic attribute "
"access is required, such as when the attribute name is determined at "
"runtime. Do not use them for known attributes or use default values to hide "
"a missing required attribute; express optional fields explicitly in the "
"interface."
msgstr ""
"优先直接访问和赋值属性（ ``obj.value`` 、 ``obj.value = value`` "
"）。只有需要动态访问，例如属性名在运行时确定时，才使用 ``getattr`` 、 ``setattr`` "
"。不要将它们用于已知属性，也不要用默认值掩盖缺失的必需属性；可选字段应在接口中明确表达。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:266
msgid ""
"Give each piece of state and validation one owner. Consumers should use the "
"owner's contract instead of repairing results or maintaining duplicate "
"state. Cache derived values only when their lifetime and invalidation are "
"clear; do not expose mutable cached results for callers to modify "
"accidentally."
msgstr ""
"每项状态和验证都应只有一个负责方。使用方应遵循其约定，而不是自行修补结果或维护重复状态。只有派生值的生命周期和失效方式明确时才缓存，不要暴露可能被调用方意外修改的可变缓存结果。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:269
msgid ""
"Keep backend selection at shared dispatch boundaries. Use established types,"
" configuration, and capability contracts instead of inferring behavior from "
"class-name strings."
msgstr "在共享分派边界选择后端。使用既有类型、配置和能力约定，不要根据类名字符串推断行为。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:271
msgid ""
"Keep physics and rendering responsibilities separate and resolve "
"construction requirements before finalization. See :doc:`/source/developer-"
"tools/scene_data_providers` for geometry ownership and "
":doc:`/source/developer-tools/add_physics_backend` for backend integration."
msgstr ""
"分开物理与渲染职责，并在最终构建完成前解决构建要求。几何归属见 :doc:`/source/developer-"
"tools/scene_data_providers` ，后端集成见 :doc:`/source/developer-"
"tools/add_physics_backend` 。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:274
msgid ""
"Prefer existing project dependencies and the standard library. Do not add "
"dependencies or compatibility layers for hypothetical future uses."
msgstr "优先使用项目已有依赖和标准库。不要为假设中的未来用途添加依赖或兼容层。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:278
msgid "Array Operations and Runtime Cost"
msgstr "数组操作与运行开销"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:280
msgid ""
"Review allocations, copies, synchronization, and recomputation in code that "
"runs per step, reset, or environment. Costs that are small for one "
"environment can dominate a large batch."
msgstr "检查每步、每次重置或每个环境执行的代码中的分配、复制、同步和重复计算。单个环境中很小的开销，在大批次中可能占主要部分。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:283
msgid ""
"Preserve slices through APIs that support them. Materialize indices only at "
"a consumer that requires them, reusing cached device indices when available."
" Preserve the selector's ordering and device contract."
msgstr "支持切片的 API 应保留切片，只有使用方要求具体索引时才生成索引数组，并尽量复用缓存的设备索引。保留选择器的顺序和设备约定。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:285
msgid ""
"Allocate arrays directly with the required value, dtype, and device. Prefer "
"``torch.full`` or ``wp.full`` over filling through Python lists, arithmetic "
"on temporary arrays, or a round trip through another library."
msgstr ""
"直接按所需值、dtype 和设备分配数组。优先使用 ``torch.full`` 、 ``wp.full`` ，而不是通过 Python "
"列表填充、对临时数组做算术，或经由另一库来回转换。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:287
msgid ""
"Remove redundant copies and ``contiguous()`` calls only after checking "
"layout and ownership requirements. Do not mutate caller-owned inputs unless "
"the API explicitly promises an in-place operation."
msgstr ""
"只有检查布局与归属要求后，才移除多余复制和 ``contiguous()`` 调用。除非 API 明确承诺原地操作，否则不要修改调用方所有的输入。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:289
msgid ""
"Batch operations when supported. Avoid Python loops over environments and "
"unnecessary host/device transfers or scalar reads that synchronize the "
"device in hot paths."
msgstr "支持时使用批量操作。在热点路径中，避免通过 Python 循环遍历环境，以及不必要的主机与设备传输，或会同步设备的标量读取。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:291
msgid ""
"Allocate expensive optional buffers on first use when their lifecycle "
"permits it. Account for graph capture: any required allocation must happen "
"before capture when the allocator requires it."
msgstr "生命周期允许时，开销较大的可选缓冲区可在首次使用时分配。还要考虑计算图捕获：如果分配器有此要求，必需分配必须在捕获前完成。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:295
msgid "Naming and Documentation"
msgstr "命名与文档"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:297
msgid ""
"Use ``snake_case`` for functions, methods, and CLI arguments. Keep related "
"public symbols discoverable through consistent prefixes and use existing API"
" vocabulary."
msgstr "函数、方法和命令行参数使用 ``snake_case`` 。通过一致的前缀使相关公共符号易于发现，并沿用已有 API 词汇。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:299
msgid ""
"Use concrete types where practical, built-in collection annotations such as "
"``list[str]``, and ``X | None`` for optional values. Keep argument and "
"return types in signatures, without repeating them in docstrings."
msgstr ""
"可行时使用具体类型、 ``list[str]`` 等内置集合注解，以及表示可选值的 ``X | None`` "
"。参数和返回类型放在签名中，不在文档字符串重复。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:302
msgid ""
"Document public APIs with Google-style docstrings. State physical units "
"inline, for example ``Particle positions [m], shape [N, 3]``. Use ``[m or "
"rad, depending on joint type]`` for mixed joint quantities. Document "
"coordinate frames and array shapes where relevant; indices, counts, and "
"flags do not need physical units."
msgstr ""
"公共 API 使用 Google 风格文档字符串。物理单位直接写在描述中，例如 ``Particle positions [m], shape [N, "
"3]`` 。混合关节量使用 ``[m or rad, depending on joint type]`` "
"。适用时说明坐标系和数组形状；索引、计数和标志不需要物理单位。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:306
msgid ""
"Keep comments brief and selective. Explain intent, non-obvious constraints, "
"or edge cases that the code alone cannot make clear. Avoid narrating "
"implementation steps or repeating what an expression does. Readability "
"comments, section markers, and headings that help organize a file are "
"welcome."
msgstr ""
"注释保持简短、有选择性。解释代码本身无法说明的意图、不明显约束或边界情况，不要逐步叙述实现，也不要重复表达式作用。欢迎有助于组织文件的可读性注释、章节标记和标题。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:309
msgid ""
"Describe the current contract in code comments. Put migration instructions "
"and descriptions of old behavior in public migration documentation or "
"changelog entries, rather than leaving a history of refactoring in the "
"implementation. Retain historical context only when it explains a constraint"
" that still affects correctness."
msgstr ""
"代码注释描述当前约定。迁移说明和旧行为描述应放在公共迁移文档或变更日志中，不要在实现内留下重构历史。只有历史背景能解释仍影响正确性的约束时，才保留它。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:313
msgid ""
"Update public documentation with API changes and verify technical claims "
"against the implementation."
msgstr "API 改变时同步更新公共文档，并根据实现核实技术说明。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:316
msgid "Code Structure"
msgstr "代码结构"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:318
msgid ""
"We follow a specific structure for the codebase. This helps in maintaining "
"the codebase and makes it easier to understand."
msgstr "我们遵循特定的代码库结构。这有助于维护代码库并使其更易于理解。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:321
msgid ""
"Keep short expressions on one line within the configured limit and break "
"longer expressions at meaningful boundaries. Keep loop headers focused on "
"iteration; unpack bulky nested records in the body. Prefer descriptive names"
" to new acronyms. Reuse matching sequences or mappings with ``*``/``**`` "
"instead of unpacking and rebuilding them; do not introduce packing "
"containers or reflective assignment just to shorten code."
msgstr ""
"在配置的长度限制内，短表达式写在一行；长表达式在有意义的边界换行。循环头只关注迭代，复杂嵌套记录在循环体内解包。优先使用描述性名称，避免新缩写。通过 "
"``*`` / ``**`` 复用匹配的序列或映射，不要解包后重建；也不要仅为缩短代码而引入打包容器或反射赋值。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:327
msgid "In a Python file, we follow the following structure:"
msgstr "在一个 Python 文件中，我们遵循以下结构："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:338
msgid ""
"Imports are sorted by Ruff through ``uv run isaaclab -f``. The groups are "
"``__future__``, standard library, third-party packages, Omniverse runtime "
"packages, Isaac Lab packages, and local relative imports; the exact package "
"groups are configured in ``pyproject.toml``. Let the formatter apply this "
"order. Use relative imports within the same package when the target is at "
"most three leading dots away (for example, ``from ...utils import math as "
"math_utils``). Use absolute imports for deeper targets, other packages, and "
"modules that run as scripts with an ``if __name__ == \"__main__\":`` block."
msgstr ""
"通过 ``uv run isaaclab -f`` ，由 Ruff 排序导入。分组依次为 ``__future__`` "
"、标准库、第三方包、Omniverse 运行时包、Isaac Lab 包和本地相对导入；具体包分组在 ``pyproject.toml`` "
"中配置，由格式化器应用顺序。同一包内、目标最多需要三个前导点时，使用相对导入，例如 ``from ...utils import math as "
"math_utils`` 。更深目标、其他包，以及包含 ``if __name__ == \"__main__\":`` "
"并作为脚本运行的模块，使用绝对导入。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:345
msgid ""
"Prefer module-level imports. A local import is appropriate when it defers an"
" optional backend or simulator dependency until the selected runtime path "
"needs it. Keep configuration imports usable before simulator startup and "
"avoid repeating runtime initialization already owned by the package. To deal"
" with circular imports, use the :obj:`typing.TYPE_CHECKING` variable. Please"
" refer to the `Circular Imports`_ section for more details."
msgstr ""
"优先在模块层导入。局部导入适用于将可选后端或仿真器依赖推迟到所选运行路径确实需要时。配置导入应能在仿真器启动前使用，不要重复包已负责的运行时初始化。循环导入可使用"
" :obj:`typing.TYPE_CHECKING` 处理，详情见 `循环导入 <Circular Imports_>`_ 。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:350
msgid ""
"Public export modules in ``__init__.py`` are an exception to the above: they"
" use :func:`~isaaclab.utils.module.lazy_export` instead of traditional "
"imports. See the `Lazy Loading & Module Exports`_ section for details."
msgstr ""
"``__init__.py`` 中的公共导出模块是例外：使用 :func:`~isaaclab.utils.module.lazy_export` "
"，而非传统导入。详情见 `延迟加载与模块导出 <Lazy Loading & Module Exports_>`_ 。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:354
msgid ""
"Pass ``ProxyArray`` objects directly to Warp kernels. Keep one proxy per "
"owned array, without parallel ``_ta``, ``_warp``, or ``_torch`` attributes; "
"timestamped array caches can own the proxy in ``data``. Use explicit native "
"access only where the receiving API requires it."
msgstr ""
"直接向 Warp 核函数传入 ``ProxyArray`` 对象。每个自有数组只保留一个代理，不要并行保存 ``_ta`` 、 ``_warp`` 或 "
"``_torch`` 属性；带时间戳的数组缓存可在 ``data`` 中持有代理。只有接收 API 要求时，才显式访问原生数组。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:358
msgid ""
"Python does not have a concept of private and public classes and functions. "
"However, we follow the convention of prefixing the private functions and "
"classes with an underscore. The public functions and classes are the ones "
"that are intended to be used by the users. The private functions and classes"
" are the ones that are intended to be used internally in that file. "
"Irrespective of the public or private nature of the functions and classes, "
"we follow the Style Guide for the code and make sure that the code and "
"documentation are consistent."
msgstr ""
"Python "
"没有私有和公共类和函数的概念。然而，我们遵循用下划线作为私有函数和类前缀的约定。公共函数和类是供用户使用的函数和类。私有函数和类是旨在在该文件内部使用的函数和类。无论函数和类是公共还是私有的，我们都遵循代码的风格指南，并确保代码和文档一致。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:365
msgid "When a class is warranted, order its members as follows:"
msgstr "确实需要类时，按以下顺序组织成员："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:381
msgid ""
"The rule of thumb is that the functions within the classes are ordered in "
"the way a user would expect to use them. For instance, if the class contains"
" the method :meth:`initialize`, :meth:`reset`, :meth:`update`, and "
":meth:`close`, then they should be listed in the order of their usage. The "
"same applies for private functions in the class. Their order is based on the"
" order of call inside the class."
msgstr ""
"经验法则是类中的函数按照用户期望使用它们的方式排序。例如，如果类包含方法 :meth:`initialize`, :meth:`reset`, "
":meth:`update`, 和 :meth:`close`, "
"然后它们应该按照使用顺序列出。私有函数在类中也适用相同的规则。他们的顺序基于在类内部调用的顺序。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:387
msgid ""
"Include only the members a class needs; this ordering is not a checklist of "
"methods to implement. For classes that own resources, expose explicit "
"cleanup through ``close()`` or a context manager."
msgstr "只包含类所需的成员；这一顺序不是要求实现所有方法的清单。持有资源的类，应通过 ``close()`` 或上下文管理器提供显式清理。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:0
msgid "Minimal function example"
msgstr "最小函数示例"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:397
msgid "Circular Imports"
msgstr "循环导入"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:399
msgid ""
"Circular imports happen when two modules import each other, which is a "
"common issue in Python. You can prevent circular imports by adhering to the "
"best practices outlined in this `StackOverflow post "
"<https://stackoverflow.com/questions/744373/circular-or-cyclic-imports-in-"
"python>`__."
msgstr ""
"循环导入发生在两个模块相互导入时，这是 Python 中常见的问题。您可以通过遵循在此 `StackOverflow post "
"<https://stackoverflow.com/questions/744373/circular-or-cyclic-imports-in-"
"python>`__ 中概述的最佳实践来防止循环导入。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:403
msgid ""
"In general, it is essential to avoid circular imports as they can lead to "
"unpredictable behavior."
msgstr "一般来说，避免循环导入是至关重要的，因为它们可能导致不可预测的行为。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:405
msgid ""
"However, in our codebase, we encounter circular imports at a sub-package "
"level. This situation arises due to our specific code structure. We organize"
" classes or functions and their corresponding configuration objects into "
"separate files. This separation enhances code readability and "
"maintainability. Nevertheless, it can result in circular imports because, in"
" many configuration objects, we specify classes or functions as default "
"values using the attributes ``class_type`` and ``func`` respectively."
msgstr ""
"然而，在我们的代码库中，我们在子包级别遇到了循环导入。这种情况是由于我们特定的代码结构所导致的。我们将类或函数及其相应的配置对象组织到不同的文件中。这种分离增强了代码的可读性和可维护性。然而，它可能导致循环导入，因为在许多配置对象中，我们使用属性"
" ``class_type`` 和 ``func`` 分别指定类或函数作为默认值。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:411
msgid "To address this, we use two complementary techniques:"
msgstr "为解决这一问题，采用两种互补方式："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:413
msgid ""
"**Resolvable strings** — Store ``class_type`` and ``func`` as "
"``{DIR}``-based strings (e.g. ``\"{DIR}.sensor:Sensor\"``) so the "
"implementation module is never imported at config construction time. The "
"string is resolved to the actual class (via "
":class:`~isaaclab.utils.string.ResolvableString`) on invocation or attribute"
" access that needs the implementation. Initialize any required runtime "
"before triggering resolution."
msgstr ""
"**可解析字符串** ：将 ``class_type`` 和 ``func`` 存为基于 ``{DIR}`` 的字符串，例如 "
"``\"{DIR}.sensor:Sensor\"`` ，避免构建配置时导入实现模块。调用或访问需要实现的属性时，通过 "
":class:`~isaaclab.utils.string.ResolvableString` 将字符串解析为实际类。触发解析前，先初始化所需运行时。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:418
msgid ""
"**TYPE_CHECKING guards** — Import the implementation class under "
"`typing.TYPE_CHECKING "
"<https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.TYPE_CHECKING>`_ so "
"that IDEs and type checkers can provide autocomplete on the type annotation "
"without triggering a runtime import."
msgstr ""
"**TYPE_CHECKING 保护** ：在 `typing.TYPE_CHECKING "
"<https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.TYPE_CHECKING>`_ "
"条件下导入实现类，使 IDE 和类型检查器可根据类型注解补全，而不触发运行时导入。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:422
msgid ""
"See the `Resolvable Strings`_ and `Lazy Loading & Module Exports`_ sections "
"for full examples of both patterns."
msgstr ""
"两种方式的完整示例见 `可解析字符串 <Resolvable Strings_>`_ 和 `延迟加载与模块导出 <Lazy Loading & "
"Module Exports_>`_ 。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:426
msgid "Configuration Operations"
msgstr "配置操作"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:428
msgid ""
"Use :func:`~isaaclab.utils.instantiate` to construct the implementation "
"selected by a config:"
msgstr "使用 :func:`~isaaclab.utils.instantiate` 构建配置所选择的实现："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:442
msgid ""
"``instantiate`` passes the config as the first constructor argument, "
"followed by any additional arguments. It does not copy configs, construct "
"nested configs, or cache instances. Resource sharing remains the "
"responsibility of ``SimulationContext.get_or_create_backend``."
msgstr ""
"``instantiate`` 将配置作为构造函数第一个参数，后接额外参数。它不复制配置、不构建嵌套配置，也不缓存实例。资源共享仍由 "
"``SimulationContext.get_or_create_backend`` 负责。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:446
msgid ""
"``clone`` and ``replace`` return new configurations, preserving fields "
"explicitly marked as borrowed. ``update_from_dict`` updates an existing "
"configuration in place. ``validate`` checks required fields and runs nested "
"``validate_config`` hooks. Prefer these functions in new code; the existing "
"``cfg.copy()``, ``cfg.replace(...)``, ``cfg.validate()``, ``cfg.to_dict()``,"
" ``cfg.from_dict(...)``, and ``cfg.class_type(cfg, ...)`` calls remain "
"supported without deprecation. The longer function names ``class_to_dict`` "
"and ``update_class_from_dict`` also remain supported."
msgstr ""
"``clone`` 和 ``replace`` 返回新配置，保留显式标记为借用的字段； ``update_from_dict`` 原地更新现有配置； "
"``validate`` 检查必需字段，并运行嵌套的 ``validate_config`` 钩子。新代码优先使用这些函数。现有 "
"``cfg.copy()`` 、 ``cfg.replace(...)`` 、 ``cfg.validate()`` 、 "
"``cfg.to_dict()`` 、 ``cfg.from_dict(...)`` 和 ``cfg.class_type(cfg, ...)`` "
"调用仍受支持，未弃用。较长名称 ``class_to_dict`` 和 ``update_class_from_dict`` 也仍受支持。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:454
msgid "Lazy Loading & Module Exports"
msgstr "延迟加载与模块导出"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:456
msgid ""
"Use **lazy loading** for public package exports so that importing a top-"
"level package (e.g. ``import isaaclab.sensors``) does not eagerly pull in "
"heavyweight dependencies like ``pxr``, ``omni``, or ``scipy``. This is "
"critical because config classes must be constructable *before* "
"``SimulationApp`` is launched."
msgstr ""
"公共包导出使用 **延迟加载** ，使导入顶层包（例如 ``import isaaclab.sensors`` ）不会立即引入 ``pxr`` 、 "
"``omni`` 或 ``scipy`` 等大型依赖。这很关键，因为配置类必须能在 ``SimulationApp`` 启动 *之前* 构建。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:461
msgid ""
"We follow `SPEC 1 — Lazy Loading of Submodules and Functions "
"<https://scientific-python.org/specs/spec-0001/>`__ and use the `lazy_loader"
" <https://pypi.org/project/lazy-loader/>`__ library (endorsed by NumPy, "
"SciPy, scikit-image, scikit-learn, NetworkX) with ``.pyi`` type-stub files. "
"The stub is the **single source of truth** for both IDE autocomplete and "
"runtime lazy loading."
msgstr ""
"我们遵循 `SPEC 1：子模块与函数的延迟加载 <https://scientific-python.org/specs/spec-0001/>`__"
" ，结合 ``.pyi`` 类型存根使用 `lazy_loader <https://pypi.org/project/lazy-loader/>`__"
" 库（获 NumPy、SciPy、scikit-image、scikit-learn、NetworkX 推荐）。存根是 IDE "
"自动补全和运行时延迟加载的 **唯一权威定义** 。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:467
msgid "**Standard pattern for public export modules:**"
msgstr "**公共导出模块的标准模式：**"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:476
msgid "With a corresponding type stub adjacent to it:"
msgstr "旁边放置对应的类型存根："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:486
msgid "Key rules for ``.pyi`` stubs:"
msgstr "``.pyi`` 存根的主要规则："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:488
msgid ""
"The ``__all__`` list at the top marks names as public re-exports (per `PEP "
"484 <https://peps.python.org/pep-0484/#stub-files>`__)."
msgstr ""
"顶部 ``__all__`` 列表将名称标为公共重新导出项，符合 `PEP 484 "
"<https://peps.python.org/pep-0484/#stub-files>`__ 。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:490
msgid ""
"Group imports from the same submodule on one line. Use parenthesized multi-"
"line imports if the line exceeds 100 characters."
msgstr "来自同一子模块的导入放在一行；超过 100 字符时，用括号进行多行导入。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:492
msgid ""
"Use **relative imports** (``from .something import ...``) for local "
"submodule symbols. Absolute wildcard imports (``from pkg import *``) are "
"only used for cross-package fallbacks (see below)."
msgstr ""
"本地子模块符号使用 **相对导入** （ ``from .something import ...`` ）。绝对通配导入（ ``from pkg "
"import *`` ）只用于跨包回退，见下文。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:495
msgid "Include the standard Isaac Lab license header."
msgstr "包含标准 Isaac Lab 许可文件头。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:497
msgid ""
"**Cross-package fallback** — for modules that re-export names from another "
"package (e.g. task MDP modules that delegate to ``isaaclab.envs.mdp``), add "
"a wildcard import for the external package in the ``.pyi`` stub:"
msgstr ""
"**跨包回退** ：对于重新导出其他包名称的模块，例如委托到 ``isaaclab.envs.mdp`` 的任务 MDP 模块，在 ``.pyi`` "
"存根中添加外部包的通配导入："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:511
msgid ""
"The ``__init__.py`` stays the same as the standard pattern — just "
"``lazy_export()`` with no arguments:"
msgstr "``__init__.py`` 与标准模式相同，只调用无参数的 ``lazy_export()`` ："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:521
msgid ""
"At runtime, ``lazy_export`` parses the ``.pyi`` stub and uses the absolute "
"wildcard import (``from isaaclab.envs.mdp import *``) as a fallback: any "
"name not found in the local submodules is looked up in the specified "
"package. This also gives type checkers and IDEs full visibility into the re-"
"exported symbols."
msgstr ""
"运行时， ``lazy_export`` 解析 ``.pyi`` 存根，并将绝对通配导入 ``from isaaclab.envs.mdp import"
" *`` 作为回退：本地子模块中找不到的名称，会到指定包中查找。这也使类型检查器和 IDE 能完整识别重新导出的符号。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:526
msgid ""
"**Relative wildcard re-exports** — the stub can also use ``from .submodule "
"import *`` to eagerly export all public names from a local submodule. This "
"is resolved at import time (not lazily). A large or frequently changing API "
"alone does not justify eager imports."
msgstr ""
"**相对通配重新导出** ：存根还可使用 ``from .submodule import *`` "
"，立即导出本地子模块的全部公共名称。这在导入时解析，并非延迟加载。仅 API 规模较大或频繁变化，并不足以成为立即导入的理由。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:532
msgid ""
"Relative wildcard re-exports bypass lazy loading and eagerly import every "
"public name from the submodule at package init time. In general, we advise "
"against using them unless absolutely necessary. Prefer listing explicit "
"named imports in the stub so that the public API surface is clear, "
"reviewable, and remains lazily loaded."
msgstr ""
"相对通配重新导出绕过延迟加载，在包初始化时立即导入子模块的全部公共名称。一般不建议使用，除非确有必要。优先在存根中列出明确的具名导入，使公共 API "
"清晰、便于审阅，并保持延迟加载。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:545
msgid "**Ensuring .pyi stubs are distributed**"
msgstr "**确保分发 .pyi 存根**"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:547
msgid ""
"Declare stub files in the package's ``pyproject.toml`` so they are included "
"in distributions:"
msgstr "在包的 ``pyproject.toml`` 中声明存根文件，将它们包含在分发包中："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:554
msgid ""
"Keep this configuration in packages that provide lazy export stubs. The pre-"
"commit ``insert-license`` hook is configured to add license headers to "
"``.pyi`` files automatically (``\\.(pyi?|ya?ml)$``)."
msgstr ""
"提供延迟导出存根的包应保留此配置。pre-commit 的 ``insert-license`` 钩子已配置为自动给 ``.pyi`` 文件添加许可头（"
" ``\\.(pyi?|ya?ml)$`` ）。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:558
msgid "Resolvable Strings"
msgstr "可解析字符串"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:560
msgid ""
"When a config field needs to reference a class or callable that depends on "
"the simulator runtime, store it as a "
":class:`~isaaclab.utils.string.ResolvableString` rather than a direct "
"reference. This avoids eagerly importing heavyweight modules (``omni``, "
"``pxr``, etc.) at config construction time. Invocation or attribute access "
"that needs the implementation triggers resolution; the caller must "
"initialize any required runtime first. Resolution does not itself wait for "
"``SimulationApp``, and workflows without Kit need not launch it."
msgstr ""
"配置字段需要引用依赖仿真器运行时的类或可调用对象时，存为 "
":class:`~isaaclab.utils.string.ResolvableString` ，而非直接引用。这样可避免构建配置时立即导入 "
"``omni`` 、 ``pxr`` 等大型模块。调用或访问需要实现的属性时会触发解析，调用方必须先初始化所需运行时。解析本身不会等待 "
"``SimulationApp`` ，不依赖 Kit 的工作流也无需启动它。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:567
msgid ""
"You can use either the ``{DIR}`` shorthand or a fully-qualified module path:"
msgstr "可使用 ``{DIR}`` 简写或完整限定模块路径："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:581
msgid ""
"The config machinery expands ``{DIR}`` to the package of the field's "
"defining class (e.g. ``isaaclab.sensors.my_sensor``), without importing the "
"referenced implementation. Prefer ``{DIR}`` for references within the same "
"package since it stays correct across renames and moves."
msgstr ""
"配置机制将 ``{DIR}`` 展开为定义该字段的类所在的包，例如 ``isaaclab.sensors.my_sensor`` "
"，而不导入被引用实现。同一包内的引用优先使用 ``{DIR}`` ，因为重命名和移动后仍能保持正确。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:585
msgid ""
"For the type annotation (``type[Sensor]``), import the class under a "
"``TYPE_CHECKING`` guard so that the IDE can still provide autocomplete "
"without triggering a runtime import:"
msgstr ""
"类型注解 ``type[Sensor]`` 所需类，应在 ``TYPE_CHECKING`` 条件下导入，使 IDE 仍能补全，而不触发运行时导入："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:597
msgid "Config + Implementation File Split"
msgstr "分开配置与实现文件"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:599
msgid ""
"For components with configuration classes, keep the configuration and "
"runtime implementation in separate files so importing configuration does not"
" load heavy runtime dependencies. This pattern does not require introducing "
"a class or configuration object for a stateless function:"
msgstr "具有配置类的组件，应将配置与运行时实现放在不同文件，使导入配置不会加载大型运行时依赖。这一模式并不要求为无状态函数引入类或配置对象："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:611
msgid ""
"``__init__.py`` — uses ``lazy_export()`` to lazily load names from the stub:"
msgstr "``__init__.py`` ：通过 ``lazy_export()`` 延迟加载存根中的名称："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:620
msgid ""
"``__init__.pyi`` — declares the public API for both IDE autocomplete and "
"lazy loading:"
msgstr "``__init__.pyi`` ：声明供 IDE 补全和延迟加载使用的公共 API："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:630
msgid ""
"``sensor_cfg.py`` — pure data; references the implementation class by "
"resolvable string to avoid importing it:"
msgstr "``sensor_cfg.py`` ：纯数据，通过可解析字符串引用实现类，避免导入："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:648
msgid ""
"``sensor.py`` — the implementation; imports runtime dependencies only when "
"needed:"
msgstr "``sensor.py`` ：实现部分，只在需要时导入运行时依赖："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:663
msgid "Type-hinting"
msgstr "类型提示"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:665
msgid ""
"Use specific type hints in function signatures and class attributes. "
"Describe meaning, units, shapes, and constraints in docstrings without "
"repeating the annotated types:"
msgstr "函数签名和类属性使用具体类型提示。文档字符串描述含义、单位、形状和约束，不重复已注解类型："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:682
msgid ""
"Prefer built-in collection types such as ``list[str]`` and ``dict[str, "
"int]``."
msgstr "优先使用 ``list[str]`` 、 ``dict[str, int]`` 等内置集合类型。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:683
msgid "Use ``X | None`` for optional values."
msgstr "可选值使用 ``X | None`` 。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:684
msgid ""
"Use ``TYPE_CHECKING`` and deferred annotations when types require runtime-"
"only imports."
msgstr "类型需要仅运行时可用的导入时，使用 ``TYPE_CHECKING`` 和延迟注解。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:686
msgid ""
"Annotate functions that return no value with ``-> None``. Omit an "
"unnecessary ``Returns:`` section from their docstrings."
msgstr "无返回值函数标注 ``-> None`` ，文档字符串省略不必要的 ``Returns:`` 章节。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:690
msgid "Documenting the code"
msgstr "编写代码文档"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:692
msgid ""
"Write documentation that lets a caller use the API without reading its "
"implementation."
msgstr "文档应使调用方无需阅读实现，即可使用 API。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:694
msgid ""
"State the behavior first, then explain constraints, defaults, and relevant "
"failure modes."
msgstr "先说明行为，再解释约束、默认值和相关失败情况。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:695
msgid ""
"Document units, coordinate frames, shapes, and ownership or mutation of "
"inputs and returned data."
msgstr "说明单位、坐标系、形状，以及输入和返回数据的归属或修改行为。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:696
msgid ""
"Explain non-obvious design constraints in brief comments near the relevant "
"code."
msgstr "在相关代码附近，用简短注释解释不明显的设计约束。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:697
msgid ""
"Use a small example when it clarifies usage. Avoid repeating the signature "
"or narrating each operation."
msgstr "小示例有助于说明用法时，可提供示例。避免重复签名或逐项叙述操作。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:698
msgid ""
"Use plain language and active voice; remove repetition and vague qualifiers."
msgstr "使用平实语言和主动表达，删除重复及含糊限定词。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:699
msgid ""
"Update documentation when behavior changes and check examples against the "
"current implementation."
msgstr "行为变化时更新文档，并根据当前实现检查示例。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:703
msgid "Unit Testing"
msgstr "单元测试"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:705
msgid ""
"We use `pytest <https://docs.pytest.org>`__ for unit testing. Keep coverage "
"lean and fast by giving each contract one primary test owner at the "
"strongest observable boundary. Start with existing coverage at that boundary"
" and extend it when it can clearly cover the changed behavior."
msgstr ""
"我们使用 `pytest <https://docs.pytest.org>`__ "
"进行单元测试。在最能体现行为的边界，为每个约定指定一个主要测试负责方，保持覆盖精简、快速。先查看该边界现有覆盖；如果能明确覆盖修改后的行为，优先扩展现有测试。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:709
msgid ""
"Apply the authoring gate and retention criteria in the `test-audit skill "
"<../../../skills/developer/test-audit/SKILL.md>`__ when adding, changing, "
"reviewing, or pruning tests. It maintains the detailed criteria for deciding"
" whether a test earns its cost."
msgstr ""
"新增、修改、审阅或精简测试时，采用 `test-audit 技能 <../../../skills/developer/test-"
"audit/SKILL.md>`__ 中的编写门槛和保留标准。它维护判断测试收益是否值得其成本的详细条件。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:713
msgid ""
"Add a test only for a distinct behavior, regression, boundary, or failure "
"mode that existing coverage does not already exercise. Formatting and "
"mechanical cleanup do not automatically require new tests. Before adding it,"
" identify the protected contract, a credible regression, and why existing "
"coverage would miss that regression. Do not add production exports, flags, "
"wrappers, or injection hooks solely to support a test; exercise the real "
"boundary instead."
msgstr ""
"只有现有覆盖未检验的独立行为、回归、边界或失败情况，才添加测试。格式调整和机械性整理不会自动要求新测试。添加前，明确保护的约定、可能发生的回归，以及现有覆盖为何发现不了。不要只为支持测试而添加生产导出、标志、包装器或注入钩子，应检验实际边界。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:718
msgid ""
"Test observable behavior and public contracts. Avoid assertions tied to "
"private implementation details or expected values computed by repeating the "
"production algorithm. Avoid assertion-free smoke tests, self-comparisons, "
"and mocks or fixtures that supply the very behavior the test claims to "
"verify."
msgstr ""
"测试可观察行为和公共约定。避免依赖私有实现细节的断言，或通过重复生产算法计算期望值。避免无断言的冒烟测试、自我比较，以及由模拟对象或测试夹具直接提供测试声称要验证的行为。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:721
msgid ""
"Verify that regression tests fail without the fix for the intended reason "
"and pass with it. Cover the bug at its owning boundary; another layer or "
"backend needs a distinct risk to justify replaying it."
msgstr "确认回归测试在没有修复时因预期原因失败，修复后通过。在错误所属边界覆盖它；在其他层或后端重复测试，需要有独立风险作为理由。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:723
msgid ""
"Keep parameter matrices and simulation fixtures focused on distinct "
"execution paths. Consolidate redundant coverage instead of adding "
"overlapping cases or rebuilding the same scene unnecessarily. Avoid "
"Cartesian products of devices, shapes, and environment counts when the axes "
"do not exercise distinct paths. Reuse the fixture that already establishes "
"the contract."
msgstr ""
"参数矩阵和仿真夹具应聚焦不同执行路径。整合多余覆盖，不要添加重叠用例或无必要地重建同一场景。如果设备、形状和环境数等维度没有检验不同路径，避免构造它们的笛卡尔积。复用已验证该约定的夹具。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:727
msgid ""
"Before removing or merging coverage, identify the proof that remains and "
"demonstrate that it fails when the contract is broken, using a focused "
"mutation of the production owner where appropriate. Preserve distinct edge "
"cases and independent API, physical, backend-parity, and packaging "
"contracts. A slow test or similar-looking assertions alone are not evidence "
"of duplication."
msgstr ""
"移除或合并覆盖前，明确剩余的验证依据，并证明约定被破坏时它会失败；适用时，对负责该行为的生产实现进行针对性变异。保留独立边界情况，以及独立的 "
"API、物理、后端一致性和打包约定。测试慢或断言看起来相似，本身不能证明重复。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:731
msgid ""
"Run the narrowest relevant test first. If an optional dependency is missing,"
" identify its project extra and retry with ``uv run --extra <extra> python "
"-m pytest ...``. For changes intended to reduce test time, measure before "
"and after on the same machine and separate kernel compilation from execution"
" time."
msgstr ""
"先运行范围最小的相关测试。如果缺少可选依赖，找到对应项目依赖组，用 ``uv run --extra <extra> python -m pytest "
"...`` 重试。以缩短测试时间为目标的修改，应在同一机器测量前后耗时，并将核函数编译与执行时间分开。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:736
msgid "Use the same commands on Linux and Windows:"
msgstr "Linux 和 Windows 使用同样命令："

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:752
msgid ""
"All of these commands exit with a nonzero code when tests fail, so a test "
"failure fails the invoking shell or CI step as well."
msgstr "这些命令在测试失败时均以非零状态退出，因此调用它们的 shell 或 CI 步骤也会失败。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:756
msgid "Tools"
msgstr "工具"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:758
msgid "We use the following tools for maintaining code quality:"
msgstr "我们使用以下工具来维护代码质量: "

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:760
msgid ""
"`pre-commit <https://pre-commit.com/>`__: Runs a list of formatters and "
"linters over the codebase."
msgstr "`pre-commit <https://pre-commit.com/>`__: 在代码库上运行格式化工具和代码检查工具的列表。"

#: source/refs/contributing.rst:761
msgid ""
"`ruff <https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/>`__: An extremely fast Python "
"linter and formatter."
msgstr ""
"`ruff <https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/>`__ ：一个极其快速的 Python 代码检查和格式化工具。"

